WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.281
One strand of collagen.

00:00:01.281 --> 00:00:03.132
Cream spreads across the skin,

00:00:03.152 --> 00:00:05.245
and stops at the surface.

00:00:05.265 --> 00:00:08.262
Powder takes a different route,
breaking apart as it goes.

00:00:08.262 --> 00:00:09.882
Where does it actually go?

00:00:09.932 --> 00:00:13.322
Under the surface, collagen
acts like a support mesh.

00:00:13.342 --> 00:00:17.664
Age slows its renewal, and ultraviolet
light helps break that mesh

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.258
down.

00:00:18.308 --> 00:00:22.379
Topically, a molecule generally
needs to be under 500 daltons

00:00:22.379 --> 00:00:23.600
to cross into skin.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.299
Collagen is around 300,000.

00:00:26.299 --> 00:00:28.092
It doesn't get through.

00:00:28.112 --> 00:00:31.010
It can still form a moisturizing
film on the surface.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.393
Skin may feel smoother,
but that's the surface,

00:00:34.393 --> 00:00:36.886
not structure below it.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:41.444
Swallow the powder, and digestion
breaks it into peptides and amino

00:00:41.464 --> 00:00:42.124
acids.

00:00:42.144 --> 00:00:45.786
They enter the bloodstream, then go
wherever the body decides they're

00:00:45.806 --> 00:00:48.062
needed most, skin, joints, tendons.

00:00:48.319 --> 00:00:50.994
No guaranteed delivery to your face.

00:00:51.244 --> 00:00:55.158
23 trials, pooled together, do
show modest gains in hydration

00:00:55.158 --> 00:00:56.881
and elasticity.

00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:58.629
But many of them were small,

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:01.271
short, and industry funded.

00:01:01.291 --> 00:01:03.186
Exclude the industry funded studies,

00:01:03.186 --> 00:01:06.394
and the benefit is no longer
statistically significant.

00:01:06.394 --> 00:01:08.513
Keep only the higher quality studies,

00:01:08.513 --> 00:01:11.870
same result. The effect stops showing up.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.874
We can't say collagen definitely works.

00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:16.630
We can't say it definitely fails, either.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:20.240
So, broad spectrum sunscreen, every day,

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.982
it's your best shield.

00:01:21.982 --> 00:01:23.165
Don't smoke.

00:01:23.315 --> 00:01:26.482
Get enough protein and vitamin
C to support the repair.

00:01:26.482 --> 00:01:32.229
And for suitable users, topical retinoids
have considerably stronger evidence for

00:01:32.327 --> 00:01:35.625
encouraging collagen
production than collagen cream.

00:01:35.645 --> 00:01:37.136
Cream can moisturize.

00:01:37.136 --> 00:01:38.335
Powder is optional.

00:01:38.355 --> 00:01:39.503
Protect first.
